  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rehabilitating basic services andbuilding resilience of community in Aleppo-SIDA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to enhance resilience and well -being in Aleppo&apos;s As -Safira district by improving sustainable access to Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) services, strengthening livelihoods, and fostering social cohesion. It targets 88,640 conflict -affected individuals, including Internally Displaced People (IDPs) and Returnees. The project will be adapted, and specific interventions will be identified and tailored in close coordination with community members and relevant authorities. The interventions include rehabilitating water infrastructure, irrigation systems, and bakeries while providing tailored training to local committees and farmers. Expected outcomes include increased agricultural productivity, reduced waterborne diseases, and improved socio -economic stability, aligning with national recovery and resilience priorities.</narrative>
  </description>
